[node name="Berserker" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1_berserker")
villain_name = "BERSERKER"
; Designer, 2026-07-25: "much tankier and damage dealer, should also move
; fast." HP 725 -> 1600 (past Dark Mage's 1450, so he now reads as the durable
; villain rather than the squishy one); damage 10 -> 24 per swing, kept on the
; same slow 1.1s interval so he stays a heavy-hitter with telegraphed swings
; instead of a fast grinder; move_speed 80 -> 135, which is ABOVE the hero
; move speed of 95 — during a charge phase he now closes on and outruns a
; fleeing hero instead of trailing behind one.
; Difficulty pass 2026-07-26 (Designer: level 2 way harder — "berserk is more
; aggressive and tanky"). HP 1600 -> 2000 before stage_2_config's villain_hp_mult
; (1.4 -> 1.9), so effective HP goes 2240 -> 3800; damage 24 -> 32 on the same
; telegraphed 1.1s swing; detect_range 120 -> 170 so he peels onto a passing
; hero instead of walking by.
;
; Freeze removal 2026-07-26 (Designer): the charge/recover cycle is gone — he
; pursues 100% of the time now instead of 4.5s-in-5.5s (~82%). Two numbers move
; with it, both sized off that duty cycle rather than guessed:
;   move_speed 140 -> 115. His AVERAGE closing speed was 140 x 0.82 = 115; at
;     100% uptime, 115 reproduces it exactly. Still above the hero's 90, so he
;     runs down a fleeing hero — he just no longer does it in bursts.
;   damage 32 -> 27. The swing itself never paused (he could attack during
;     recovery), but he now spends materially more time standing in melee range
;     because heroes no longer get a beat to peel off. ~15% off the swing pays
;     for that extra in-range uptime, on the same telegraphed 1.1s interval the
;     last two passes deliberately preserved.
; HP is untouched: the ask was to balance his attacks, and his durability was
; never what the freeze was paying for.
;
; Swing rate 2026-07-26 (Designer: "attack heroes more often"): attack_interval
; 1.1 -> 0.8. This is the first pass that gives up the slow telegraph on
; purpose — at 27 damage he goes from 24.5 to 33.8 damage/sec on a single
; target, above even the 29.1 he did before the freeze came out. Damage is left
; at 27 rather than dropped again to hold that line: the ask was more frequent
; hits, and 0.8s is still slow enough to read as a wind-up rather than a grind.
max_hp = 2000.0
damage = 27.0
attack_interval = 0.8
attack_range = 26.0
detect_range = 170.0
move_speed = 115.0
body_color = Color(0.851, 0.224, 0.224, 1)
body_radius = 32.0
